## Merge Reconciliation & Synthesis

### 1. Faucet Implementation (Real Testnets Only)
Per your directive, the platform will **never simulate** a faucet for live testnets. Instead:

- **Address Generation & Persistence**  
  The app now includes `ethers.js` (loaded from CDN). When TESTNET mode is active, a “🪪 Generate Test Wallet” button creates a **real Ethereum Sepolia address** using `ethers.Wallet.createRandom()`. The private key is **not stored** (the user must fund the address externally; this is for test validation only). The public address is saved in `localStorage` so it persists across sessions.

- **Faucet Request**  
  A “🚰 Get Test ETH” button opens a **new browser tab** pointing to the official Sepolia faucet (`https://faucet.sepolia.dev/`) with the generated address pre‑filled via the `?address=` query parameter (when supported). As an embedded webpage view would be blocked by X‑Frame‑Options on almost all faucets, opening a separate tab is the only reliable method. The user can then complete the CAPTCHA and receive real test ETH.  
  *If the faucet format changes, the user can manually copy the address displayed on the screen.*

- **Testnet Balance Check**  
  When TESTNET is active, the app displays the balance of the testnet wallet by querying the Sepolia RPC (using a public endpoint) via `ethers`. This ensures you can verify that funds have arrived before attempting live testnet trades.

### 2. Full Feature Reconciliation
The two codebases are merged without loss:

